/// @file groups.dox
/// Doxygen-only file (not compiled) declaring ndl's top-level module groups.
/// Nothing here is C++; @ingroup tags elsewhere in the real headers attach
/// classes/functions to these groups so the generated docs have a "Modules"
/// index alongside the plain class list.

/// @defgroup core_image Core Image Types
/// Image<T,DIM>, its owning and bit-packed variants, and the zero-copy view
/// operations (view()/slice()/swap_axes()/mirror()) shared by all of them.

/// @defgroup morphology_filtering Morphology & Filtering
/// erode()/dilate()/median_filter()/percentile_filter()/threshold()/otsu_threshold()/
/// invert() -- free functions (morphology.h) over any minimal-interface image type
/// (Image or PackedBitImage), a toolkit built on top of Image rather than part of it --
/// plus the structuring-element helpers (make_box_kernel()/make_cross_kernel()) and
/// BorderMode.

/// @defgroup convolution Convolution
/// convolve()/gaussian_blur() -- free functions (convolution.h), a toolkit built on
/// top of Image rather than part of it, same relationship morphology.h's functions
/// have. Kept separate from Morphology & Filtering above: both groups walk a kernel
/// over every position, but convolution combines the values under it into a weighted
/// sum, where morphology picks a single one (min/max/percentile) -- a different
/// family of operation, even though they share BorderMode and the same kernel-tap
/// machinery underneath.

/// @defgroup visualize Visualize
/// bar_chart()/heatmap() (visualize.h) -- render any 1D/2D minimal-interface
/// numeric array as a real image (a bar chart or a greyscale intensity image
/// respectively), scaled to the array's own max value. Exists so nothing else in
/// this library needs its own one-off ASCII-art rendering: histogram_image()
/// (Histogram, below) is a thin dispatch straight to these, not separate drawing
/// code.

/// @defgroup histogram Histogram
/// Histogram<VDIM>, histogram_equalize(), and histogram_image() (histogram.h) --
/// bins the joint distribution of VDIM co-occurring scalar values (VDIM==1 is the
/// ordinary single-channel histogram; VDIM==2/3/... are joint/co-occurrence
/// histograms), generalizing over VDIM the same way Image<T,DIM> generalizes over
/// spatial dimension DIM. otsu_threshold() (Morphology & Filtering, above) is
/// built on Histogram<1> internally; histogram_image() renders a Histogram<1>/
/// Histogram<2> as a real bar chart/heatmap via Visualize, above.

/// @defgroup distance_transform Distance Transform
/// distance_transform()/distance_transform_squared() (distance_transform.h) -- the
/// exact squared Euclidean distance transform (Felzenszwalt & Huttenlocher), computed
/// via one 1D lower-envelope-of-parabolas pass per axis, the same "one 1D pass per
/// axis" structure fftn() (FFT, below) uses. Always measures distance to the nearest
/// background (false/zero) position; invert() (Morphology & Filtering, above) flips
/// that to distance-to-nearest-foreground when that's what's wanted instead.

/// @defgroup summed_area_table Summed-Area Table
/// summed_area_table()/rectangle_sum() (summed_area_table.h) -- builds an integral
/// image via one prefix-sum pass per axis (again the same per-axis structure fftn()
/// uses), then answers "what's the sum over this arbitrary rectangle" in O(1) via
/// inclusion-exclusion over the table's own corners, regardless of the rectangle's
/// size. box_blur(), also here, is the payoff built on top: an O(1)-per-pixel
/// (2*radius+1)^DIM average via one rectangle_sum() query per pixel, with real
/// BorderMode support (Clamp/Wrap/Reflect, the same enum convolve()/erode() share) --
/// implemented by building one border-extended copy of the source up front (via the
/// same detail::kernelTapCoord() those use) so every downstream query lands on an
/// always-in-bounds table position, rather than by making rectangle_sum() itself
/// border-aware.

/// @defgroup fft FFT
/// Complex/real power-of-two FFT (FFT, FFTReal), arbitrary-size FFT via Bluestein's
/// algorithm (FFTBluestein), and the N-dimensional Image-based entry points
/// (fftn()/ifftn()) most callers actually want.

/// @defgroup matrix Matrix
/// Fixed-size, compile-time-dimensioned NxN matrices and the geometric transforms
/// (scale/translate/rotate/project) built on them.

/// @defgroup image_io Image I/O
/// Loading and saving images in bitmap/PNG/JPEG/DICOM/NRRD/raw formats.

/// @defgroup utilities Utilities
/// Small standalone helpers (Timer, code_timer(), change_endian()) not specific
/// to image processing.
